# Build artifacts (HDF5 data stores are generated from the CSVs; not committed)
*.h5
*.hdf5

# ...except the bundled national-tier stores, which ship inside the package.
# These are small (~MBs), built by scripts/build_hdf5.py, and committed so that
# `pip install` is self-contained. Larger subnational tiers stay uncommitted.
!starsim_data/data/*.h5

# ...and the contact stores that are fetched on demand rather than bundled: committed
# here, outside the package, and downloaded by fetch() from a pinned commit.
!fetched/*.h5

# UN WPP demographics source. The normalized CSVs (raw_data/demographics/wpp_*.csv)
# and README are tracked as the demographic source of truth; only the bulky raw
# downloads (xlsx/gz/zip) and logs are scratch and ignored.
raw_data/demographics/*.xlsx
raw_data/demographics/*.csv.gz
raw_data/demographics/*.zip
raw_data/demographics/*.log

# great-docs build directory (ephemeral; great-docs.yml is the committed source)
great-docs/

# Quarto's execution cache. Deliberately not committed: letting CI execute the code cells
# afresh means the docs build also checks that the documented examples still run.
_freeze/
